  "scope": "The product adapter owns the released 64 KiB continuation encode/decode and static size/restorability gates. VM public codecs are exact reexports; journal and restore callers retain original ordered private-stage aliases. Six legacy/adapter entry comparisons over 70 operations and 18 defects produce 7560 comparisons; 17 binding forms, versions 0 through 12 and two group-owner states produce 2652 comparisons. Expected outputs use independent frozen frame admission, canonical token checks, canonical source checks and pre-existing frozen capped writers, not the migrated codec. Existing 980 malformed-decode cases now also use the frozen static-admission oracle. Four direct adapter tests verify exact wire round trips, mutable-data revalidation, size/JSON order, exact-limit whitespace, recursive native preflight and static group metadata without a VM. The memory consumer rejects changed live images, refuses a decoded group member without complete journal ownership and preserves the next allocated effect identity; actual completion still fences restore of consumed state. Observe imports its encoding function from the adapter. Daemon production and test consumers use adapter protocol DTOs with an explicit direct dependency; only Vm and DEFAULT_FUEL remain imported from the evaluator in its debugger. All 170 daemon library tests pass after permitting the temporary local HTTPS/Unix socket listeners blocked by the sandbox; no remote server deployment is involved. The native source export is unchanged and reverified. Native durable recovery and full extraction remain incomplete, and decoding never authenticates or executes a saved image.",
